{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When you till</b>. Some say that ונוד is from the root קונן, like \"לנוד לו\" (Job 2:11). In my opinion, נד is like נע, and similar to it, \"הנה ארחיק נדוד\" (Psalms 55:8)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads ונוד here as related to נד ('to wander'), not lamentation; he cites Job 2:11 where לנוד is traditionally understood as 'to comfort/console,' but some take it from נוד = לקונן ('to lament')."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:20.705508627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}